{
  "_comment": "Single source of truth for tunables. JSON rather than YAML on purpose: Go's standard library parses it with no dependency, and the browser parses it natively via fetch().json() — a YAML file would need a third-party parser on both sides. Every limit can be overridden by an env var (see config.go) so a Fly deploy can be retuned without a rebuild.",

  "limits": {
    "_comment": "Guardrails for a public URL. Sessions are held in RAM, so every one of these bounds memory. Generous for real meetings, tight enough that one caller cannot exhaust a 256MB machine.",
    "maxSessions": 500,
    "maxClientsPerSession": 60,
    "maxConnectionsPerIP": 25,
    "maxSessionsPerIP": 10,
    "trustProxyHeaders": true
  },

